# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is normal on a Windows checkout, but these scripts are read by
# bash INSIDE a Linux container (tests/docker/*.sh) or by Git Bash driving one. A CRLF
# checkout makes container bash fail with `set: -: invalid option` and
# `syntax error near unexpected token $'do\r'` — which reads as a broken test, not as a
# line-ending problem. Cost a debugging round on 2026-09-12.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.cjs text eol=lf
